   "text": {
    "L1": "At first, Prabhat could not bear losing, so he played only when sure of winning.",
    "L2": "In the badminton match, Surya played brilliantly while Prabhat kept the score.",
    "L3": "When Surya looked away, Prabhat changed the scoreboard and won by cheating.",
    "L4": "The win felt empty. Prabhat could not sleep, and Surya did not even feel bad about losing.",
    "L5": "Prabhat then watched Surya enjoy every game, whether he won or lost.",
    "L6": "Prabhat realised that a game should be enjoyed for its own sake, not only for the score.",
    "L7": "His actions showed the change: he played, joked and gained a great sporting spirit.",
    "L8": "That is why the story is called Change of Heart. Now choose what Prabhat learnt."
   },
